qvac-fabric[xdna-backend] requires system XRT >= 2.25 and an IRON Python
interpreter in QVAC_XDNA_IRON_PYTHON. Export QVAC_XDNA_IRON_VERSION with the
installed mlir-aie release and preserve QVAC_XDNA_IRON_PYTHON in the vcpkg
build environment.

The module uses the system libstdc++ ABI and embeds the absolute XRT library
path in RUNPATH. Consumers must track the system toolchain in their Linux
x64 triplet before binary-cache lookup (VCPKG_KEEP_ENV_VARS alone does not
hash values):

    if(PORT STREQUAL "qvac-fabric" OR PORT STREQUAL "xrt")
      list(APPEND VCPKG_ENV_PASSTHROUGH XILINX_XRT QVAC_XDNA_IRON_VERSION)
      if(NOT "$ENV{XILINX_XRT}" STREQUAL "")
        file(TO_CMAKE_PATH "$ENV{XILINX_XRT}" _xrt_root)
      else()
        set(_xrt_root "/opt/xilinx/xrt")
      endif()
      if(EXISTS "${_xrt_root}/share/cmake/XRT/xrt-config.cmake")
        list(APPEND VCPKG_HASH_ADDITIONAL_FILES "${_xrt_root}/share/cmake/XRT/xrt-config.cmake")
      endif()
    endif()

CUDA and XDNA share ggml-base-libstdcxx, a PIC static archive compiled
against libstdc++. The final CUDA module links its runtime statically; XDNA
links it dynamically to match XRT. Both use the same CMake configure.

No NPU is required to compile. The XDNA module and its kernel artifacts must
be installed together. Hosts without XRT skip the optional module.

qvac-fabric[coreml-ffn] (macOS) builds the Qwen3.8-27B Core ML FFN sidecar;
llama_supports_coreml_ffn() then returns true. A common_params with
coreml_ffn set turns it on in common_init_from_params. Static consumers link
the CoreML, Foundation and Metal frameworks. The first load compiles 4.5-9 GB
of Core ML programs into the cache directory (coreml_ffn_cache, default
$LLAMA_CACHE/coreml-ffn or ~/Library/Caches/llama.cpp/coreml-ffn). See
docs/coreml-ffn.md in qvac-fabric-llm.cpp.
